'' T21, RUN: a dynamic array never REDIM-ed is "not dimensioned" -- runtime error 18, exit
'' 18, as fbc reports it. Its bounds are zero-filled, so a bounds check alone would pass
'' index 0 and read through a null pointer: the first version of the T21 fix did exactly
'' that and crashed. fb_ArrayDimensionChk runs first and catches it.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -exx -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/boundchk-dyn-undim.bas -o tests/codegen/boundchkdynundim.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/boundchkdynundim.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/boundchkdynundim.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 18
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: runtime error 18 (array not dimensioned) at line 2 of
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 'A' not dimensioned and array elements are not allocated
